==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[endictment]]

===Etymology===
18th century Latinized respelling of {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|endytement||lang=enm|action of accusing}}, from {{etyl|xno|en}} {{term|enditement|lang=fro}}, from {{term|enditer|lang=fro}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ɪnˈdaɪt.mənt/}}
* {{audio|en-us-indictment.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# {{context|legal|lang=en}} An official formal [[accusation]] for a criminal [[offence]], or the process by which it is brought to a [[jury]]. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
# {{context|legal|lang=en}} The official legal document outlining the [[charge]]s concerned. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
# {{context|countable|uncountable|lang=en}} An [[accusation]] of wrongdoing; a [[criticism]] or [[condemnation]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}

